    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: netfilter: nf_tables: prevent nf_skb_duplicated corruption (CVE-2024-49952)\n\n* kernel: net/smc: reject CHID-0 ACCEPT that matches an empty ism_dev slot (CVE-2026-64048)\n\n* kernel: bpf: Support for hardening against JIT spraying (CVE-2026-64508)\n\n* kernel: x86/bugs: Enable IBPB flush on BPF JIT allocation (CVE-2026-64507)\n\n* kernel: net/iucv: fix use-after-free of a severed iucv_path (CVE-2026-68140)\n\n* kernel: nvmet-rdma: handle inline data with a nonzero offset (CVE-2026-72129)\n\n* kernel: i3c: master: svc: bound IBI payload to the requested max_payload_len (CVE-2026-80951)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* RHEL is missing support for conntrack zone filtering in dump/delete requests (9.4.z) (JIRA:RHEL-272448)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
